{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>peace-offering sacrifices to HaShem, etc.</b> It should have said ״וְזָבְחוּ אוֹתָם זִבְחֵי״ and so on. Or perhaps the Master intended to show the endearment of holiness with which He endears His people, and He said <b>for peace-offering sacrifices</b> — these are offerings of those who share at one table together, children and their fathers, and this is the meaning of His saying <b>peace-offerings to HaShem, them</b>: and the word ״them״ refers back to the children of Israel who sacrifice, mentioned at the beginning of the verse — not to the animals being sacrificed. And on this matter alone the soul is loosened from its sheath and rises to the service of El with a surrender of soul, without any sensation, because of the intensity of the sweetness felt in the aspect of His love — may He be blessed — in the soul that feels a taste of the pleasantness of His endearment. And all this is slight in comparison to what is incumbent upon us to do, in relation to that which He — may He be blessed — has prepared beforehand for us in the aspect of the delight of His cherishing us and the exaltedness with which He exalts the people of His holiness."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The phrase מִנַּרְתֵּקָהּ (from its sheath) is translated hyper-literally; the imagery is of the soul drawn from its bodily housing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:57:43.808597365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}